/** @page pgsqlcopyguide COPY Protocol Support

    @tableofcontents

    The pgsql driver supports PostgreSQL's \c COPY protocol for maximum-throughput bulk inserts. When
    a <tt>COPY ... FROM STDIN</tt> SQL statement is executed with a hash-of-lists argument, the driver
    streams data directly to the server using PostgreSQL's escaped text COPY format, bypassing SQL
    statement parsing for each row.

    The COPY protocol is the fastest way to load data into PostgreSQL but does not support upserts
    or \c RETURNING clauses. Use \ref pgsqlbulkdml "array binds" when those features are needed.

    @par Example: Using COPY via PgsqlSqlUtil
    @code{.py}
%requires PgsqlSqlUtil

Datasource ds("pgsql:user/pass@db%host");
PgsqlTable table(ds, "my_table");

on_success ds.commit();
on_error ds.rollback();

# copyInsert() uses the COPY protocol internally
int rows_copied = table.copyInsert({
    "id": (1, 2, 3, 4, 5),
    "name": ("Alice", "Bob", "Charlie", "Dave", "Eve"),
    "created": (now(), now(), now(), now(), now()),
});
printf("Copied %d rows\n", rows_copied);
    @endcode

    @par Example: Direct COPY FROM STDIN
    @code{.py}
# pass a hash-of-lists as the argument to a COPY FROM STDIN statement
int rows = ds.exec("COPY my_table (id, name) FROM STDIN", {
    "id": (1, 2, 3),
    "name": ("Alice", "Bob", "Charlie"),
});
    @endcode

    @par Example: Opt-in native COPY via BulkSqlUtil
    @code{.py}
%requires BulkSqlUtil
%requires SqlUtil

Datasource ds("pgsql:user/pass@db%host");
SqlUtil::AbstractTable table = (new SqlUtil::Table(ds, "my_table")).getTable();
BulkSqlUtil::BulkInsertOperation op(table, {
    "bulk_load": True,       # require native COPY; "auto" falls back when ineligible
    "block_size": 1000,
});
on_success {
    op.flush();
    op.endStream();
    ds.commit();
}
on_error {
    op.discard();
    ds.rollback();
}
map op.queueData($1), rows.iterator();
    @endcode

    When this opt-in path is selected, the driver starts one <tt>COPY ... FROM STDIN</tt> operation,
    sends each BulkSqlUtil block with one c PQputCopyData() call, and finalizes or aborts it from the
    driver-neutral begin/rows/end protocol.  The legacy direct-SQL COPY detection remains available
    unchanged for compatibility.  Native COPY is insert-only and cannot provide c RETURNING values
    or row callbacks; BulkSqlUtil rejects those combinations with c "bulk_load": c True and uses its
    ordinary insert path with c "bulk_load": c "auto".

    @note
    - The COPY protocol does not support \c RETURNING clauses or upsert semantics
    - All list values must have the same number of elements
    - The operation is cancellable via Qore's standard I/O interruption mechanism
    - On error, the COPY operation is aborted and the transaction must be rolled back
    - COPY streams report bounded stream boundaries to a datasource mutation observer if one is
      registered; see @ref pgsqlmutationobserver
*/
